+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report
+
+Property-based tests for the public `rustybuzz` shaping API, written with
+[hegel](https://hegel.dev) (`hegeltest` dev-dependency, added with
+`--ignore-rust-version`: hegeltest's MSRV is 1.86 vs. rustybuzz's declared
+1.65). All tests live in `tests/shaping/main.rs`, module `properties`, and run
+with the standard `cargo test --test shaping properties::`.
+
+The C HarfBuzz library is not available in this environment, so differential
+testing against HarfBuzz was out of scope; all properties are standalone.
+
+Shared infrastructure: a curated list of 19 repo test fonts spanning the
+shapers (OpenType GSUB/GPOS AOTS fonts, Arabic/Nastaliq, Indic, USE, Myanmar,
+Hangul/CJK, AAT morx/kerx/trak, variable fonts), and a text generator biased
+towards single-script runs from the matching Unicode blocks with special
+characters (ZWJ/ZWNJ, variation selectors, dotted circle, tatweel, matras,
+NUL, newlines) and fully arbitrary codepoints mixed in. Features, variations,
+directions, scripts, languages, cluster levels, buffer flags, ptem/ppem and
+pre/post contexts are all generated.
+
+## Properties tested
+
+1. **`shape_never_panics_on_arbitrary_input`** — `shape()` +
+   `GlyphBuffer::serialize` never panic for any text × font × features ×
+   variations × buffer settings × pre/post context × ptem/ppem ×
+   not-found-variation-selector glyph. (Found both bugs below.)
+2. **`shape_is_deterministic`** — identical face/text/features/settings shaped
+   twice produce identical glyph infos and positions.
+3. **`clusters_are_monotone_for_monotone_cluster_levels`** — with
+   `MonotoneGraphemes`/`MonotoneCharacters`, output clusters are
+   non-decreasing for forward directions (LTR/TTB) and non-increasing for
+   backward ones (RTL/BTT), per https://harfbuzz.github.io/clusters.html.
+4. **`cluster_values_map_to_input_char_offsets`** — every output cluster value
+   is one of the char byte offsets assigned by `UnicodeBuffer::push_str`
+   (shaping only merges/copies clusters), for all three cluster levels.
+5. **`nonempty_text_shapes_to_at_least_one_glyph`** — non-empty text never
+   shapes to an empty glyph buffer (missing codepoints fall back to .notdef);
+   `REMOVE_DEFAULT_IGNORABLES` is excluded since it legitimately deletes
+   glyphs.
+6. **`shaping_with_mutated_fonts_never_panics`** — fonts with random byte
+   flips (up to 16) and/or truncation either fail `Face::from_slice` or shape
+   and serialize without panicking.
+7. **`reusing_buffer_after_clear_matches_fresh_buffer`** —
+   `GlyphBuffer::clear()` (documented buffer-reuse path) followed by shaping a
+   second text gives byte-identical results to a fresh `UnicodeBuffer`.
+8. **`spec_string_parsers_never_panic`** — `Feature`/`Variation`/`Language`/
+   `Direction` `FromStr` impls return `Err` rather than panicking on arbitrary
+   and spec-shaped strings.
+9. **`feature_from_str_parses_constructed_feature_strings`** — round-trip of
+   the documented feature spec grammar (`kern`, `+kern`, `-kern`, `kern=2`,
+   `kern[3:5]=2`, `=on`/`=off`, negative indices) into the documented
+   tag/value/start/end, including the documented negative-value wrapping.
+10. **`guess_segment_properties_is_idempotent`** — always resolves a
+    non-`Invalid` direction and a second call never changes
+    direction/script/language, with and without preset direction/script.
+
+Plus two deterministic pinned reproducers for the bugs found (see below):
+`known_failure_set_variations_non_finite_value_panics` and
+`known_failure_not_found_variation_selector_glyph_above_u16_max`.
+
+## Test results
+
+- All 10 property tests pass at the default 100 cases and at an exploratory
+  10x run (`test_cases = 1000`).
+- The 2 `known_failure_*` tests fail deterministically on every run, pinning
+  the two real bugs found. They are the only failures in the entire suite
+  (lib: 187 passed; shaping: 2156 passed, 2 pinned failures).
+- Liveness was verified by temporarily inverting the expected value in
+  property 9 (hegel shrank to the minimal `"AAAA"` counterexample) and by the
+  organic failures of properties 1/4/5 during development, which shrank to
+  minimal inputs before being pinned.
+- Pre-existing, unrelated: `examples/shape.rs` does not compile on this
+  platform (aarch64 Linux: `libc::setlocale` expects `*const u8` c_char, the
+  example casts to `*const i8`). Verified on the clean tree before any
+  changes. Not touched, since fixing bugs was out of scope.
+
+## Suspected bugs
+
+Both were found by `shape_never_panics_on_arbitrary_input`, shrunk by hegel,
+then pinned as deterministic failing tests. Both are debug-build panics
+reachable from the safe public API with no documented contract excluding the
+input; not fixed per instructions.
+
+1. **`Face::set_variations` panics on non-finite variation values.**
+   `Variation { tag: wght, value: f32::INFINITY }` (or NaN) on a variable font
+   that has the axis panics via ttf-parser's
+   `debug_assert!(val.is_finite())` in `f32_bound` (`parser.rs:916`), reached
+   through `ttf_parser::Face::set_variation` → `VariationAxis::normalized_value`.
+   `Variation::value` documents no finiteness requirement, and
+   `Variation::from_str` is the obvious untrusted-input source; HarfBuzz
+   clamps out-of-range values instead. Pinned:
+   `known_failure_set_variations_non_finite_value_panics`.
+
+2. **`set_not_found_variation_selector_glyph` values above `u16::MAX` break
+   the `glyph_id <= u16::MAX` guarantee.** The setter takes `u32` (HarfBuzz
+   glyph ids are 32-bit) but `deal_with_variation_selectors`
+   (`src/hb/ot_shape.rs`) writes the raw value into
+   `hb_glyph_info_t::glyph_id`, whose rustdoc guarantees `<= u16::MAX`. In
+   debug builds `as_glyph()` (`src/hb/buffer.rs:246`) panics, e.g. from
+   `GlyphBuffer::serialize`; in release builds the documented guarantee is
+   silently violated and the glyph id is truncated at use sites. Repro: text
+   `"\u{200C}\u{FE00}"` with a font lacking the variation selector in cmap and
+   `set_not_found_variation_selector_glyph(0x10000)`. Pinned:
+   `known_failure_not_found_variation_selector_glyph_above_u16_max`.
+
+After pinning, the sibling generators exclude exactly these two regions
+(non-finite variation values; not-found glyph > `u16::MAX`), with comments
+referencing the pinned tests.
+
+## Unsound properties abandoned
+
+Considered during design and rejected before/without committing:
+
+- **`push_str` ≡ repeated `add(c, byte_offset)`** — tautological: `push_str`
+  is implemented as exactly that loop, so the property could not fail.
+- **Pre/post context does not change the number of glyphs** — unsound:
+  context legitimately changes shaping (e.g. Arabic joining forms picked by
+  surrounding context), and nothing pins the glyph count.
+- **"Fresh buffer equals reused buffer without re-applying settings"** — the
+  stronger version of property 7 is unsound: `clear()` deliberately resets
+  direction/script/language/cluster level (and deliberately keeps
+  `BufferFlags`, matching HarfBuzz's `hb_buffer_clear_contents`), so settings
+  are re-applied on both sides of the comparison.
+- Property 5 (non-empty output) was initially suspect because AAT `morx` can
+  delete glyphs, which could legitimately empty a buffer; empirically it held
+  across the AAT fonts at 10x cases, so it was kept unrestricted apart from
+  the documented `REMOVE_DEFAULT_IGNORABLES` exclusion. If a future failure
+  shows all-deleted morx output, the property (not the code) should be
+  revisited.
+
+## Skill feedback
+
+- The Rust reference was accurate throughout: the `hegeltest`-package /
+  `hegel`-crate naming, the MSRV `--ignore-rust-version` note, the builder
+  form for borrowing fixtures (used here for the preloaded font data — the
+  `#[hegel::test]` free-function form could not have borrowed it), the "no
+  char generator" idiom, and the single-use-generator gotcha all matched
+  reality exactly.
+- The "keep a failing test that pins a real bug + exclude that region from
+  siblings with a comment" guidance worked well here: one broad no-panic
+  property found two independent bugs in the first default-count run, and the
+  workflow cleanly separated them.
+- Minor friction: draws made inside plain helper functions print as opaque
+  `draw_N` in counterexamples (as the reference warns). For this test suite,
+  mapping `draw_1 = 1` back to "font index 1" required reading the draw order;
+  `#[hegel::composite]` would name them but cannot borrow the font fixture, so
+  helper functions were still the right call. A way to label individual draws
+  (`tc.draw_labelled("font_idx", ...)`) would have helped.
+- The liveness-check advice ("passing hegel tests print nothing") and the 10x
+  exploratory-run advice were both cheap and worthwhile; the 10x run gave
+  extra confidence in the monotone-cluster and non-empty-output properties
+  that had non-obvious soundness arguments (morx deletion, backward
+  directions).
